    "stem": "Evaluate \\(\\lim_{z \\to 3}\\left[\\dfrac{z(2z-3)-9}{z^{2}-4z+3}\\right]\\)",
    "solution": "If we substitute \\(z = 3\\) in numerator and denominator, we get \\(z(2z-3)-9 = 0\\) and \\(z^{2}-4z+3 = 0\\)\nSo \\((z-3)\\) is a factor in the numerator and denominator.\n\\(\\lim_{z \\to 3}\\left[\\dfrac{z(2z-3)-9}{z^{2}-4z+3}\\right] = \\lim_{z \\to 3}\\left[\\dfrac{2z^{2}-3z-9}{z^{2}-4z+3}\\right]\\)\n\\(= \\lim_{z \\to 3}\\left[\\dfrac{(z-3)(2z+3)}{(z-3)(z-1)}\\right]\\)\n\\(= \\lim_{z \\to 3}\\left[\\dfrac{(2z+3)}{(z-1)}\\right]\\) ...[As \\(z \\to 3\\), \\(z-3 \\ne 0\\)]\n\\(= \\dfrac{2(3)+3}{3-1}\\)\n\\(= \\dfrac{9}{2}\\)"
  },
