    "subtopic": "Method of Factorization",
    "difficulty": "MODERATE",
    "stem": "Evaluate \\(\\lim_{x \\to 1}\\left[\\dfrac{x^{3}+x^{2}-5x+3}{x^{2}-1}\\right]\\)",
    "solution": "In this case \\((x-1)\\) is a factor of the numerator and denominator\nTo find another factor we use synthetic division.\nNumerator: \\(x^{3}+x^{2}-5x+3\\)\n\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | -5 | 3 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|  |  | 1 | 2 | -3 |\n|  | 1 | 2 | -3 | 0 |\n\n\\(\\therefore x^{3}+x^{2}-5x+3 = (x-1)\\left(x^{2}+2x-3\\right)\\)\nDenominator: \\(x^{2}-1 = (x+1)(x-1)\\)\n\\(\\lim_{x \\to 1}\\left[\\dfrac{x^{3}+x^{2}-5x+3}{x^{2}-1}\\right]\\)\n\\(= \\lim_{x \\to 1}\\left[\\dfrac{(x-1)\\left(x^{2}+2x-3\\right)}{(x+1)(x-1)}\\right]\\)\n\\(= \\lim_{x \\to 1}\\left[\\dfrac{x^{2}+2x-3}{x+1}\\right]\\) ...[As \\(x \\to 1\\), \\(x-1 \\ne 0\\)]\n\\(= \\dfrac{1+2-3}{1+1} = 0\\)"
  },
