    "stem": "Evaluate \\(\\lim_{x \\to 0}\\left(\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}+1}}{x^{2}}\\right)\\)",
    "solution": "Put \\(\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}+1} = t\\), \\(x^{2}+1 = t^{3}\\)\n\\(\\therefore x^{2} = t^{3}-1\\), as \\(x \\to 0\\), \\(t \\to 1\\)\n\\(\\lim_{x \\to 0}\\left(\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}+1}}{x^{2}}\\right) = \\lim_{t \\to 1}\\left(\\dfrac{(1-t)}{\\left(t^{3}-1\\right)}\\right)\\)\n\\(= \\lim_{t \\to 1}\\left(\\dfrac{-(t-1)}{(t-1)\\left(t^{2}+t+1\\right)}\\right)\\)\n\\(= \\lim_{t \\to 1}\\left(\\dfrac{-1}{t^{2}+t+1}\\right)\\) ...[As \\(t \\to 1\\), \\(t-1 \\ne 0\\)]\n\\(= \\dfrac{-1}{1+1+1} = -\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)"
  },
